{
  "name": "metro-line",
  "vibe": "A transit diagram that actually runs. Off-white #f4f4f0 map paper carries four service colours — red #d9363e, blue #2f6db5, green #3f9b57, yellow #e8b820 — as 16px rounded polylines with 45° corners and white interchange dots ringed in ink. A red train, two white windows and all, crawls its route on a six-second loop while a rule at the foot extends and resets. Barlow Condensed sets everything in caps at sign weight. The camera glides on the axes only — no rotation, no skew — so the frame pans like a map under glass. Its signature is the split-flap Morph, letters clattering over, beside a scrolling departures board, drop-in alerts and a bar gauge. Dark ink panels hold screenshots; the last beat floods red. Best for transit, logistics, delivery and city services.",
